            <ArticleTitle>Parosteal Osteosarcoma of the Distal Radius Mimicking an Osteochondroma-A Diagnostic Misadventure.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1038.e1-1038.e10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0363-5023(17)31203-0</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jhsa.2017.07.010</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of a parosteal osteosarcoma mimicking an osteochondroma with atypical clinical features, radiographic findings, and histological examination. This report serves to exemplify the importance of recognizing the similarities between these 2 entities and other peculiar features that will help to differentiate between sessile osteochondromas and parosteal osteosarcomas, to prevent misdiagnosis.</AbstractText>
